  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated multi-sector assistance to support vulnerable communities in drought-affected areas in Borena Zone, Moyale and debuluk woredas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltbrgtltspangtThis project is a multi-sectoral life-saving
response, for drought, floods and cholera-affected&#xa0;communities in Borena
Zone, Moyale and Dubuluk woredas. DPO aims to provide integrated Agriculture, WASH,
Protection and MPC activities to respond to the current high need on the
ground. Strengthen the protection system through engagement, awareness raising
and capacity building for community-based structures, protection service
providers, and other sector service providers to prevent and mitigate the risk
of violence, neglect and abuse, including SEA, while addressing barriers to
accessing protection services. Additionally, the Provision of access to clean, potable
water supply for the affected community and maintenance of outdated water
supply systems and improve the affected people&apos;s hygiene and sanitation habits
identified for WASH activities. In Agriculture, provision of agricultural
inputs (seeds) and support for livestock water point rehabilitation through
cash for work assistance. Finally, muti-purpose cash will be distributed&#xa0;to
protection service recipients in the affected communities. lt/spangtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
